{
  "ID": "GoR_Common_SimpleBattle_SignalIntercept",
  "contractName": "Signal Intercept",
  "contractDisplayStyle": "BaseCampaignNormal",
  "difficulty": 5,
  "difficultyUIModifier": 0,
  "weight": 1,
  "scope": "STANDARD",
  "finalDifficulty": 0,
  "representativeCastDefIDOverride": "castDef_ArelleJorgensson",
  "shortDescription": "Long-range sensors have detected a formation of BattleMechs moving through the remote terrain of <i>Melidron</i>. Their formation pattern, thermal profiles, and signal behavior match those of the advanced modified designs first observed during earlier encounters. Machines believed to be connected to the long since Annihilated Clan Wolverine.\n\nThese are not relics. These are active combat units. Modernized, field-tested, and hidden behind silence.\n\nEngagement is authorized. The objective is not complete destruction, but recovery of data, wreckage, or any identifying components. Transmission must be prevented at all costs. If these units withdraw intact, another chance may not come again.\n\nThey have erased their history and masked their movements. But now, the updated Wolverine-born designs have been seen in the open. They must be forced to leave something behind.",
  "longDescription": "Those are the same kind of 'Mechs we saw back at the start. Reforged Wolverines, no doubt. If we're finally seeing them out in the open, this isn't just a lucky break. It's a test. Let's not fail it.",
